hello everyone and welcome to math  simplified  i'm dr umar malik and today we will be  talking about  the signs and symptoms that you can  develop if you have a heart disease  these signs and symptoms can help you to  find out the problem in early stages  and prevent further complications our  heart pumps  blood non-stop 24 7 throughout our lives  every organ depends on the heart to  deliver fresh oxygenated blood to them  that's a lot of activity and pressure so  wear and tear is bound to happen and  certain activities can cause the heart  to face problems at some point or the  other  in this video we will not talk about  specific problems themselves  but take a look at what signs and  symptoms these problems might present  with  this will help you to be more vigilant  regarding heart diseases and  identify them early on in your life so  keeping that in mind  let's start with a simple question what  is a heart disease  heart disease are one of the leading  health risks  humanity faces today according to the  american heart association  more than one in three adults suffer  from heart diseases  and according to who around 18 million  people die  each year from heart diseases which is  an estimated 31 percent of all deaths  worldwide  here we must clarify one thing heart  disease is an umbrella term  it includes diseases such as heart  failure  coronary artery disease arrhythmias  angina  atherosclerosis and other heart related  infections  irregularities and birth defects  now keeping in mind that the heart plays  a very crucial role in our survival  it may seem that something so serious  should have warning signs  but that is not the case according to  the center of disease control cdc  50 of people who die from coronary heart  disease  didn't even knew they had it because of  lack of symptoms  it is possible to develop heart diseases  without knowing it  as you go about your daily life so  it's important to know the early signs  and symptoms of heart disease  as well as the risk factors so that you  can get treatment  early and prevent more serious heart  problems  let's first talk about what are the risk  factors for developing heart diseases  according to the center of disease  control and prevention  nearly half of all the americans both  men and women  have three or more risk factors for  heart disease  let's take a look at few of these risk  factors  so that you can modify and control them  if possible  number one age growing older increases  your risk of damaged and narrowed  arteries and weakens your heart muscles  number two gender men are generally  at a greater risk of developing heart  disease  the risk for women increases after  menopause  number three a family history of heart  disease increases your risk of coronary  artery disease  especially if your parent developed it  at an early stage  number four smoking smoking is a very  important and modifiable risk factor for  heart disease  nicotine tightens your blood vessels and  carbon monoxide present in the cigarette  smoke  can damage their inner lining making  them more susceptible to atherosclerosis  heart attacks are also more common in  smokers than in non-smokers  number 5 poor diet is also a risk factor  a diet that is high in fat salt  sugar and cholesterol can contribute to  the development of heart diseases  number six uncontrolled high blood  pressure can result in hardening and  thickening of your arteries  which leads to narrowing of vessels  through which the blood flows  number seven high levels of cholesterol  in your blood can increase the risk of  plaque formation and atherosclerosis in  the blood vessels of your heart  number eight if you have diabetes this  also increases your risk of developing  heart diseases  both conditions share similar risk  factors such as obesity and high blood  pressure  obesity is also a risk factor excess  weight  typically worsens other heart diseases  and also increases the risk of  developing atherosclerosis  number 10 physical inactivity and lack  of exercise  are also associated with many forms of  heart disease  number 11 excessive stress is also a  known risk factor  a combination of risk factors may also  signal impending heart disease  for example your risk of heart disease  significantly increases if you have  diabetes  and high blood pressure now let's look  at the early signs  of heart disease usually there are no  signs of heart disease  it often presents unexpectedly in the  form of a heart attack  or other serious event but there are few  important signs and symptoms that can  help you to recognize heart problems  before they become serious in the early  stages  symptoms can develop that seem like mere  annoyances  and may come and go for example you may  have  a very short episode of heart arrhythmia  which is basically  an irregular heartbeat you can  experience  difficulty in catching your breath after  moderate physical exertion like  walking up a flight of stairs you can  develop a sense of discomfort or  squeezing in your chest  that lasts for 30 minutes to a few hours  unexplained pain in your upper torso  neck  and jaw is another early symptom  a heartbeat that is faster slower or  irregular than usual can also be the  presenting symptom  you can also experience an episode of  dizziness or fainting  heart diseases that involve your blood  vessels  are often signaled by chest pain also  known as angina  shortness of breath extreme fatigue  irregular heartbeat  and you can also experience symptoms in  your hands and feet such as  tingling numbness coldness and weakness  these symptoms can be signs that your  blood vessels have narrowed  this narrowing which can be caused by  plaque buildup  makes it more difficult for your heart  to circulate oxygenated blood  throughout your body similarly heart  diseases caused by an infection of the  heart can include symptoms  like fever shortness of breath weakness  or fatigue swelling in your legs or  abdomen  changes in your heart rhythm dry or  persistent cough  skin rashes or unusual spots  now let's discuss about some signs of a  heart attack  a myocardial infarction also known as  heart attack occurs when the heart  disease has reached at a point where  blood  flow to the muscles of the heart  decreases it becomes  so low that the heart is unable to meet  the energy demands of the muscles of the  heart itself  the most common sign of a heart attack  is just discomfort that  includes tight squeezing intense  pressure on your chest  which may or may not be associated with  chest pain  this discomfort may also be present in  your arms  back neck abdomen or jaw  during a heart attack you may also have  shortness of breath profuse sweating for  no apparent reason  nausea and lightheadedness  knowing the signs of a heart attack is  one of the most important things you can  do to safeguard your cardiac health  your ability to recover from one of  these serious events  depends on how quickly you receive  treatment for them  it can be difficult to determine if you  are experienced symptoms of a heart  attack  never ignore symptoms as normal always  seek immediate medical attention if you  are concerned about  any symptoms that you have it's crucial  to reduce your risk factors for heart  disease  whether you have symptoms or not  schedule  regular checkups even if you think you  are in excellent health  establishing a baseline for your health  will help you  and your doctor address any concerns  that arise in the future  reducing risk factors and modifying your  life habits  go a long way in decreasing your risk of  suffering from heart diseases  and also lessens the impact if you  already have one  so friends with this we come to the end  of this video  we talked about the various scientists  risk factors for heart diseases  this is a series of videos about signs  and symptoms of various diseases of our  body  comment in the section below and tell us  what topics  you would like us to cover next we at  math simplified are committed to  bringing you the latest and updated  content  if you like what we do support us by  sharing this video with someone whom  you might think find it useful you can  also become a member of a youtube  channel or support us through patreon  the links are in the description below  thank you so much for watching  and stay safe
 

